container 600px

I believe the public might give arguments against copyright and patent law more consideration if they saw not just many arguments, but arguments from _many people_.

This is the start of that collection.

In the process of creating this collection I learned of Stephan Kinsella's Anti-IP Reader, which is the best collection I've seen to date, and how I first discovered a number of these essays.
 https://stephankinsella.com/ip-reader/ Anti-IP Reader

***

I put together this site independently and did not ask any of the authors for permission. Although I hope they find it helpful and useful, their inclusion does not in any way mean they endorse this project. Any shortcomings or mistakes are mine.

***

The Overton Window theory predicts a range of arguments currently politically acceptable to the mainstream population. The Overton Window shifts, and then lawmakers shift the law.
 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overton_window Overton Window

In a Tweet heard round the world, on April 11, 2025, two of the wealthiest capitalists in the world said "delete all IP law". Tens of thousands agreed.
 https://x.com/jack/status/1910829254214115681 a Tweet heard round the world

I hope this is a sign that support for the abolishment of copyright and patent law is starting to go viral.

* - Breck Yunits
5/1/2025

